course: dictionary
lesson: 9189
title: Political words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe how a country is run. A socialist is a person who believes that important businesses, land and wealth should be shared or controlled by the people or the government, so that everyone is treated more equally. Look at the words around it for clues: «The socialist party wants public services to be run for everyone.» The clue is that the party wants things run for everyone, so the word is about fairness.
explain: Socialist can also describe things, so it works as an adjective. «Socialist ideas» are ideas about sharing wealth and power. «A socialist government» is a government that follows socialist ideas. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Politics has other words for different beliefs. Conservative and liberal are other political views, and each one says something different about money, work and fairness. You do not need to know them all yet. Read the sentence around the word for clues, and use a dictionary when the clues are not enough.
explain: Some groups have used the word in their name. «The National Socialists, who ruled Germany from 1933 to 1945» is one example. A name does not always show what a group really did, so when a word appears in a title, check its meaning carefully.
fact: Socialist is a noun when it names a person, and an adjective when it describes something, such as socialist ideas.
fact: Socialism is the idea that important businesses, land and wealth should be shared or controlled by the people or the government.
fact: «Socialist» means believing in socialism, so that everyone is treated more equally.
fact: «Socialist party» means a political party that supports socialism.
fact: Some groups have used the word in their name, but a name does not always show what a group really did.
exercise: A socialist believes that important businesses, land and wealth should be what? | Given away to the sea | *Shared or controlled by the people or the government | Kept only by one rich family | Sold to the highest bidder
exercise: Which phrase uses socialist as an adjective, describing something? | the socialists | a socialist is a person | *socialist ideas | socialists meet on Monday
exercise: Which word names a political view, like socialist, conservative or liberal? | Barely | Ancient | Curt | *Liberal
test: In «a socialist government», what does the word tell you about the government? | It has no rules at all | *It follows socialist ideas about sharing wealth and treating people more equally | It sells everything to other countries | It is made up of only children
test: Which of these is a political view, like socialist? | *Conservative | Famished | Drooped | Luminous
exam: Why should you check a dictionary when a word is used in a group's name? | Because names are always written in capital letters | Because names are never true | Because dictionaries are always wrong | *Because a name does not always show what the group really did
